{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c495","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":165,"recorded_at":1780531400000325,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-d74b-7122-a0d5-741c9b94f857"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-d74b-7122-a0d5-741c9b94f857","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01d-d74b-7122-a0d5-741c9b94f857","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(877 line(s) above)\n878|### 4.A TerminalBackend authority and terminology\n879|\n880|TerminalBackend is a host-local presentation and delegated process-hosting\n881|module. AX alone owns Logical Session identity and lineage, Owner and AX\n882|Replica roles, leases and fencing, provider lifecycle/native identity/store,\n883|workspace materialization, Checkpoints/evidence, task-board integration, mesh\n884|replication, and takeover. A backend owns exactly one host-local\n885|<dfn>Terminal Instance</dfn>: delegated PTY/process hosting, presentation,\n886|attach/reconnect, backend-local IPC, and backend-specific process observation.\n887|\n888|An <dfn>AX Replica</dfn> is a host holding synchronized durable AX state. A\n889|<dfn>presentation replica</dfn> or <dfn>client mirror</dfn> is only a view/input\n890|client of one Terminal Instance. Presentation replication MUST NOT create an AX\n891|Replica, acquire or renew a lease, change Owner, authorize input, or publish an\n892|owner-authored event. Schemas, CLI, UI, and logs MUST NOT use these terms\n893|interchangeably.\n894|\n895|Every backend-created runtime ultimately executes exactly\n896|<code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>; a raw provider command is forbidden as a\n897|durable entry point. A backend MUST NOT interpret ownership, start or resume a\n898|provider without AX authorization, replace AX/provider/workspace/Checkpoint/\n899|task-board/mesh state, or turn attach into a lease mutation. A valid takeover\n900|or owner resume MAY bind the same Logical Session to a different conforming\n901|destination backend without clone or fork; AX emits a new immutable binding,\n902|event, and evidence and never mutates history.\n903|\n904|### 4.B Registry, identity, discovery, and trust\n905|\n906|<code>terminal_backend_id</code> is 1–128 ASCII bytes matching\n907|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*</code>. The <code>ax.</code> namespace is\n908|reserved. Canonical built-ins are <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n909|<code>ax.conpty</code>. Third parties use a stable vendor-owned namespace. No\n910|normative Superlogical ID is reserved.\n911|\n912|Terminal Backend Manifest 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no\n913|other member is permitted:\n914|\n915|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n916|| --- | --- |\n917|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest</code> |\n918|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n919|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n920|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n921|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver |\n922|| <code>protocol_versions</code> | sorted unique semver[1..32], each in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n923|| <code>platforms</code> | sorted unique enum[1..4] from <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> |\n924|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | <code>builtin_go|local_program|trusted_executable|native_runtime</code> |\n925|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest for <code>local_program</code> or <code>trusted_executable</code>; null otherwise |\n926|| <code>static_capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] whose <code>origin</code> is <code>static</code> |\n927|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest |\n928|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code>; non-empty extensions require a later contract version |\n929|\n930|Terminal Backend Probe 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable observation; no\n931|other member is permitted:\n932|\n933|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n934|| --- | --- |\n935|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe</code> |\n936|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n937|| <code>probe_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n938|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n939|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to the admitted Manifest |\n940|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver selected from the Manifest's <code>protocol_versions</code> |\n941|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | enum equal to the Manifest member |\n942|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest|null exactly equal to the Manifest member |\n943|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>, contained in the Manifest's <code>platforms</code> |\n944|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] |\n945|| <code>availability</code> | <code>available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code> |\n946|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest of the domain-separated raw generation |\n947|| <code>capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] |\n948|| <code>evidence_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..256] referencing Capability Evidence 1.0.0 |\n949|| <code>probed_at</code> | timestamp |\n950|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n951|\n952|The generation digest uses SHA-256 over UTF-8\n953|<code>ax-terminal-backend-generation-v1\\0</code> followed by the backend's\n954|host-local raw generation bytes; it neither reveals nor reconstructs that\n955|generation. Manifest-to-Probe reconciliation is the following closed rule. The\n956|Probe <code>terminal_backend_id</code>, <code>implementation_version</code>,\n957|<code>implementation_kind</code>, and <code>executable_digest</code> MUST equal\n958|the Manifest members; its <code>protocol_version</code> MUST be exactly one member\n959|of <code>protocol_versions</code>, and its <code>platform</code> MUST be exactly\n960|one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,\n961|not aggregate equality.\n962|\n963|Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability\n964|<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The\n965|declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this\n966|reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:\n967|\n968|1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a\n969|   manifest/probe mismatch.\n970|2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>\n971|   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for\n972|   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.\n973|3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a\n974|   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when\n975|   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,\n976|   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and\n977|   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and\n978|   the capability registry row.\n979|4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed\n980|   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and\n981|   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add\n982|   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.\n983|5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence\n984|   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence\n985|   requirement. The required fact mapping is\n986|   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,\n987|   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,\n988|   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,\n989|   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and\n990|   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no\n991|   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the\n992|   literal <code>true</code>.\n993|6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all\n994|   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.\n995|   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for\n996|   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting\n997|   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.\n998|\n999|A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an\n1000|error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed\n1001|relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is\n1002|<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\n1003|activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps\n1004|to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\n1005|\n1006|Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,\n1007|manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable\n1008|substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims\n1009|fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv\n1010|and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus\n1011|UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,\n1012|invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.\n1013|M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a\n1014|stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\n1015|validate the boundary.\n1016|\n1017|Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase\n1018|<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member\n1019|omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain\n1020|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1021|\n1022|Terminal Backend Protocol 1.0.0 has a closed request envelope containing\n1023|exactly <code>protocol</code> with literal\n1024|<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\n1025|<code>protocol_version</code> with exact value <code>1.0.0</code>,\n1026|<code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>operation</code>, and <code>body</code>.\n1027|Its response repeats those three identity members exactly and contains\n1028|<code>ok:true,result:&lt;operation-success-body&gt;</code> or\n1029|<code>ok:false,error:StructuredError1.3</code>, never both result and error.\n1030|Operation is one of the ten names in Section 4.C and the exact bodies are its\n1031|typed matrix. Unknown members, operations, or body variants are protocol\n1032|errors. This is an AX-controlled local adapter wire, not a stable public SDK.\n1033|\n1034|AX allocates <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>. Terminal Instance Binding\n1035|1.0.0 is the following closed immutable host-local object; no other member is\n1036|permitted:\n1037|\n1038|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1039|| --- | --- |\n1040|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding</code> |\n1041|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1042|| <code>binding_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule above |\n1043|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1044|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1045|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1046|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1047|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1048|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1049|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1050|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1051|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1052|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1053|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1054|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1055|\n1056|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1057|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1058|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1059|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1060|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1061|\n1062|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1063|\n1064|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1065|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1066|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1067|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1068|\n1069|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1070|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1071|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1072|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1073|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1074|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1075|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1076|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1077|\n1078|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1079|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1080|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1081|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1082|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1083|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1084|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1085|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1086|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1087|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1088|\n1089|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1090|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1091|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1092|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1093|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1094|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1095|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1096|\n1097|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1098|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1099|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1100|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1101|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1102|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1103|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1104|\n1105|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1106|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1107|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1108|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1109|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1110|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1111|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1112|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1113|\n1114|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1115|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1116|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1117|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1118|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1119|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1120|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1121|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1122|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1123|\n1124|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1125|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1126|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1127|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1128|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1129|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1130|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1131|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1132|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1133|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1134|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1135|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1136|\n1137|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1138|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1139|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1140|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1141|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1142|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1143|persisted or replicated.\n1144|\n1145|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1146|| --- | --- | --- |\n1147|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1148|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1149|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1150|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1151|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1152|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1153|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1154|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1155|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1156|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1157|\n1158|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1159|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1160|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1161|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1162|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1163|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1164|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1165|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1166|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1167|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1168|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1169|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1170|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1171|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1172|\n1173|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1174|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1175|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1176|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1177|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1178|transition and no side effect.\n1179|\n1180|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1181|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1182|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1183|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1184|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1185|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1186|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1187|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1188|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1189|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1190|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1191|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1192|\n1193|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1194|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1195|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1196|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1197|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1198|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1199|\n1200|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1201|\n1202|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1203|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1204|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1205|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1206|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1207|\n1208|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1209|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1210|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1211|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1212|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1213|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1214|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1215|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1216|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1217|\n1218|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1219|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1220|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1221|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1222|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1223|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1224|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1225|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1226|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1227|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1228|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1229|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1230|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1231|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1232|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1233|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1234|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1235|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1236|\n1237|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1238|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1239|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1240|member is permitted:\n1241|\n1242|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1243|| --- | --- |\n1244|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1245|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1246|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1247|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1248|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1249|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1250|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1251|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1252|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1253|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1254|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1255|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1256|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1257|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1258|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1259|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1260|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1261|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1262|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1263|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1264|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1265|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1266|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1267|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1268|\n1269|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1270|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1271|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1272|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1273|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1274|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1275|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1276|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1277|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1278|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1279|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1280|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1281|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1282|change and before activation.\n1283|\n1284|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1285|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1286|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1287|activation when policy allows.\n1288|\n1289|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n1290|\n1291|| Classification | Members and rule |\n1292|| --- | --- |\n1293|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n1294|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n1295|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n1296|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n1297|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c497","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":166,"recorded_at":1780531400000327,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-d74b-7122-a0d5-741c9b94f857"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-d74b-7122-a0d5-741c9b94f857","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b01d-d74b-7122-a0d5-741c9b94f857"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c499","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":167,"recorded_at":1780531400000329,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01dd2857699948142493b7a7d54","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(877 line(s) above)\n878|### 4.A TerminalBackend authority and terminology\n879|\n880|TerminalBackend is a host-local presentation and delegated process-hosting\n881|module. AX alone owns Logical Session identity and lineage, Owner and AX\n882|Replica roles, leases and fencing, provider lifecycle/native identity/store,\n883|workspace materialization, Checkpoints/evidence, task-board integration, mesh\n884|replication, and takeover. A backend owns exactly one host-local\n885|<dfn>Terminal Instance</dfn>: delegated PTY/process hosting, presentation,\n886|attach/reconnect, backend-local IPC, and backend-specific process observation.\n887|\n888|An <dfn>AX Replica</dfn> is a host holding synchronized durable AX state. A\n889|<dfn>presentation replica</dfn> or <dfn>client mirror</dfn> is only a view/input\n890|client of one Terminal Instance. Presentation replication MUST NOT create an AX\n891|Replica, acquire or renew a lease, change Owner, authorize input, or publish an\n892|owner-authored event. Schemas, CLI, UI, and logs MUST NOT use these terms\n893|interchangeably.\n894|\n895|Every backend-created runtime ultimately executes exactly\n896|<code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>; a raw provider command is forbidden as a\n897|durable entry point. A backend MUST NOT interpret ownership, start or resume a\n898|provider without AX authorization, replace AX/provider/workspace/Checkpoint/\n899|task-board/mesh state, or turn attach into a lease mutation. A valid takeover\n900|or owner resume MAY bind the same Logical Session to a different conforming\n901|destination backend without clone or fork; AX emits a new immutable binding,\n902|event, and evidence and never mutates history.\n903|\n904|### 4.B Registry, identity, discovery, and trust\n905|\n906|<code>terminal_backend_id</code> is 1–128 ASCII bytes matching\n907|<code>[a-z][a-z0-9]*(?:[.-][a-z0-9]+)*</code>. The <code>ax.</code> namespace is\n908|reserved. Canonical built-ins are <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n909|<code>ax.conpty</code>. Third parties use a stable vendor-owned namespace. No\n910|normative Superlogical ID is reserved.\n911|\n912|Terminal Backend Manifest 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no\n913|other member is permitted:\n914|\n915|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n916|| --- | --- |\n917|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-manifest</code> |\n918|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n919|| <code>manifest_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n920|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n921|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver |\n922|| <code>protocol_versions</code> | sorted unique semver[1..32], each in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n923|| <code>platforms</code> | sorted unique enum[1..4] from <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> |\n924|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | <code>builtin_go|local_program|trusted_executable|native_runtime</code> |\n925|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest for <code>local_program</code> or <code>trusted_executable</code>; null otherwise |\n926|| <code>static_capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] whose <code>origin</code> is <code>static</code> |\n927|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest |\n928|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code>; non-empty extensions require a later contract version |\n929|\n930|Terminal Backend Probe 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable observation; no\n931|other member is permitted:\n932|\n933|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n934|| --- | --- |\n935|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-backend-probe</code> |\n936|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n937|| <code>probe_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule below |\n938|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n939|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to the admitted Manifest |\n940|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver selected from the Manifest's <code>protocol_versions</code> |\n941|| <code>implementation_kind</code> | enum equal to the Manifest member |\n942|| <code>executable_digest</code> | digest|null exactly equal to the Manifest member |\n943|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code>, contained in the Manifest's <code>platforms</code> |\n944|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] |\n945|| <code>availability</code> | <code>available|conditional|unavailable|unknown</code> |\n946|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest of the domain-separated raw generation |\n947|| <code>capability_claims</code> | sorted by capability, unique TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim[0..16] |\n948|| <code>evidence_ids</code> | sorted unique digest[0..256] referencing Capability Evidence 1.0.0 |\n949|| <code>probed_at</code> | timestamp |\n950|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n951|\n952|The generation digest uses SHA-256 over UTF-8\n953|<code>ax-terminal-backend-generation-v1\\0</code> followed by the backend's\n954|host-local raw generation bytes; it neither reveals nor reconstructs that\n955|generation. Manifest-to-Probe reconciliation is the following closed rule. The\n956|Probe <code>terminal_backend_id</code>, <code>implementation_version</code>,\n957|<code>implementation_kind</code>, and <code>executable_digest</code> MUST equal\n958|the Manifest members; its <code>protocol_version</code> MUST be exactly one member\n959|of <code>protocol_versions</code>, and its <code>platform</code> MUST be exactly\n960|one member of <code>platforms</code>. Array-to-scalar selection is membership,\n961|not aggregate equality.\n962|\n963|Let <code>M[c]</code> be the one Manifest static claim for capability\n964|<code>c</code>, when present, and <code>P[c]</code> the one Probe claim. The\n965|declared sorted-unique constraints make a duplicate key invalid before this\n966|reconciliation runs. The complete keyed relation is:\n967|\n968|1. Every <code>M[c]</code> MUST have exactly one <code>P[c]</code>; omission is a\n969|   manifest/probe mismatch.\n970|2. <code>P[c].origin=static</code> is permitted only when <code>M[c]</code>\n971|   exists, and <code>P[c]</code> MUST then equal <code>M[c]</code> member for\n972|   member. It is a static echo, not a new observation.\n973|3. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> with an existing <code>M[c]</code> is a\n974|   generation-bound override. It is permitted only when\n975|   <code>M[c].generation_variable=true</code>; its <code>value</code> MAY differ,\n976|   while <code>generation_variable</code>, <code>dependent_operations</code>, and\n977|   <code>evidence_requirements</code> MUST remain equal to <code>M[c]</code> and\n978|   the capability registry row.\n979|4. <code>P[c].origin=probed</code> without <code>M[c]</code> is a probed\n980|   addition. It is permitted only for a capability in the closed registry, and\n981|   its three registry-derived members MUST equal that row. A Probe cannot add\n982|   a claim with <code>origin=static</code>.\n983|5. A true <code>P[c]</code> is admitted only when unexpired Capability Evidence\n984|   bound to this exact Manifest/Probe tuple satisfies every listed evidence\n985|   requirement. The required fact mapping is\n986|   <code>conformance_fixture-&gt;fixture_passed</code>,\n987|   <code>runtime_probe-&gt;runtime_probe_passed</code>,\n988|   <code>credential_sentinel-&gt;sentinel_passed</code>,\n989|   <code>provider_auth_smoke-&gt;provider_auth_passed</code>, and\n990|   <code>policy_authorization-&gt;policy_checked</code>. A false claim has no\n991|   matching Capability Evidence because Evidence <code>value</code> is the\n992|   literal <code>true</code>.\n993|6. <code>evidence_ids</code> MUST be exactly the sorted unique IDs of all\n994|   returned Capability Evidence objects used by true <code>P</code> claims.\n995|   Every referenced object MUST name exactly one present true claim; an ID for\n996|   an absent or false claim, an unreferenced returned object, conflicting\n997|   evidence, or duplicate/conflicting claims invalidates the whole Probe.\n998|\n999|A partial, malformed, stale, or failed Manifest, Probe, or evidence read is an\n1000|error, never absence or availability. Any failed equality, membership, keyed\n1001|relation, evidence binding, or evidence coverage rule is\n1002|<code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code> and fails before\n1003|activation; executable substitution or implementation drift additionally maps\n1004|to its more specific Section 15.3 code.\n1005|\n1006|Discovery completes before activation. Duplicate/ambiguous IDs,\n1007|manifest/probe disagreement, implementation drift, untrusted executable\n1008|substitution, stale generation, unknown identity/version, or unevidenced claims\n1009|fail closed. A manifest is not availability proof. External adapters use argv\n1010|and local length-prefixed framing: unsigned 32-bit big-endian byte length plus\n1011|UTF-8 JSON, at most 1 MiB, one request/response at a time. EOF, oversize,\n1012|invalid JSON, unsolicited output, or deadline expiry terminates the adapter.\n1013|M0 exposes only an internal semantic interface and conformance harness; a\n1014|stable public SDK is deferred until tmux and one materially different backend\n1015|validate the boundary.\n1016|\n1017|Manifest, Probe, Binding, and Capability Evidence IDs equal the lowercase\n1018|<code>sha256:</code> digest of RFC 8785 JCS bytes with their own ID member\n1019|omitted. A reader MUST recompute the ID before use. Manifest and Probe remain\n1020|immutable observations when later probes supersede them.\n1021|\n1022|Terminal Backend Protocol 1.0.0 has a closed request envelope containing\n1023|exactly <code>protocol</code> with literal\n1024|<code>urn:ax:protocol:terminal-backend</code>,\n1025|<code>protocol_version</code> with exact value <code>1.0.0</code>,\n1026|<code>request_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>operation</code>, and <code>body</code>.\n1027|Its response repeats those three identity members exactly and contains\n1028|<code>ok:true,result:&lt;operation-success-body&gt;</code> or\n1029|<code>ok:false,error:StructuredError1.3</code>, never both result and error.\n1030|Operation is one of the ten names in Section 4.C and the exact bodies are its\n1031|typed matrix. Unknown members, operations, or body variants are protocol\n1032|errors. This is an AX-controlled local adapter wire, not a stable public SDK.\n1033|\n1034|AX allocates <code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>. Terminal Instance Binding\n1035|1.0.0 is the following closed immutable host-local object; no other member is\n1036|permitted:\n1037|\n1038|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1039|| --- | --- |\n1040|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-instance-binding</code> |\n1041|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1042|| <code>binding_id</code> | digest computed by the identity rule above |\n1043|| <code>session_id</code> | Logical Session UUIDv7 |\n1044|| <code>host_id</code> | AX Host UUIDv7 |\n1045|| <code>host_incarnation_id</code> | UUIDv7 allocated once for the current host-agent process incarnation |\n1046|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-allocated UUIDv7 |\n1047|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1048|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to admitted Manifest and Probe |\n1049|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1, equal to the Probe |\n1050|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256]; this is the canonical bound in every containing contract |\n1051|| <code>native_reference</code> | sanitized opaque string[1..512], meaningful only to this backend on this host incarnation |\n1052|| <code>created_at</code> | timestamp |\n1053|| <code>supersedes_binding_id</code> | digest|null; null only for the first binding of this Session on this host incarnation |\n1054|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1055|\n1056|Identity MUST NOT be a PID, handle, socket, path, named pipe, URL, token, or\n1057|mutable endpoint. Binding is host/incarnation-local and does not alter Logical\n1058|Session identity. Boundary conformance cases MUST reject generation lengths 0\n1059|and 257 and accept length 256 in the Binding, Provider Protocol 3 descriptor,\n1060|operation bodies, and CLI Result 4 summary.\n1061|\n1062|### 4.C Lifecycle and operations\n1063|\n1064|Terminal Instance state is exactly <code>absent</code>, <code>creating</code>,\n1065|<code>parked</code>, <code>active</code>, <code>quiescing</code>,\n1066|<code>stopped</code>, <code>stale_fenced</code>, or <code>unavailable</code>.\n1067|This describes local hosting only; it is not a second ownership state machine.\n1068|\n1069|Every mutating request carries operation, Session, Terminal Instance and\n1070|idempotency IDs; exact backend ID/version/generation; deadline; and an expiring\n1071|AX authorization with winning lease ID/epoch. Results repeat those identities,\n1072|before/after state, side effects, evidence IDs, and one retry disposition:\n1073|<code>replay_same</code>, <code>status_first</code>,\n1074|<code>new_authorization</code>, or <code>required_operator_action</code>.\n1075|Authorization and generation are rechecked immediately before each side effect.\n1076|A deadline cancels waiting, not a committed effect.\n1077|\n1078|The closed <dfn>TerminalInstanceState</dfn> enum is the eight-state registry in\n1079|the first paragraph of this subsection. The closed\n1080|<dfn>TerminalBackendSideEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1081|<code>binding_persisted|wrapper_started|attach_client_created|input_closed|safe_boundary_observed|graceful_stop_requested|process_closed|backend_store_closed|stale_incarnation_terminated|wrapper_restored</code>.\n1082|The closed <dfn>PresentationTransport</dfn> enum is\n1083|<code>local_only|trusted_private_mesh|third_party_relay</code>. The closed\n1084|<dfn>ProviderProofKind</dfn> enum is\n1085|<code>provider_quiescence|provider_process_exit|ax_checkpoint_boundary</code>.\n1086|The closed <dfn>TerminalStatusLastEffect</dfn> enum is exactly\n1087|TerminalBackendSideEffect.\n1088|\n1089|<code>creating</code> is entered only by <code>create</code> after its durable\n1090|idempotency receipt and before its first listed side effect. An error before a\n1091|side effect restores the source state. An error after an effect whose result\n1092|cannot be proven moves the local observation to <code>unavailable</code> with\n1093|<code>status_first</code>; it MUST NOT claim <code>absent</code>. No operation\n1094|other than <code>quiesce-input</code> enters <code>quiescing</code>, and no\n1095|backend operation enters <code>stale_fenced</code>: AX fencing observation does.\n1096|\n1097|<dfn>AXAuthorization</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1098|<code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991]</code>,\n1099|<code>holder_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1100|<code>authorization_kind:create|control|force_stale|restore</code>,\n1101|<code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, <code>expires_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1102|<code>authorization_evidence_id:digest</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue;\n1103|the lease tuple MUST equal the current winning AX lease at every side effect.\n1104|\n1105|<dfn>AttachAuthorization</dfn> is a closed, ownership-neutral AX policy object\n1106|containing exactly <code>policy_evidence_id:digest</code>,\n1107|<code>authorizing_host_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1108|<code>transport:PresentationTransport</code>,\n1109|<code>input_authorized:boolean</code>, <code>issued_at:timestamp</code>, and\n1110|<code>expires_at:timestamp</code>. Expiry is strictly after issue. It authorizes\n1111|only the named presentation transport and input boolean; it contains no lease\n1112|and cannot acquire, renew, or transfer ownership.\n1113|\n1114|<dfn>MutationContext</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1115|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1116|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1117|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1118|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1119|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1120|<code>idempotency_key:string[1..256]</code>, <code>deadline_at:timestamp</code>,\n1121|and <code>authorization:AXAuthorization</code>. The key is the canonical UTF-8\n1122|encoding specified per operation below; it is not caller-chosen free text.\n1123|\n1124|<dfn>MutationResult</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1125|<code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>session_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1126|<code>terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7</code>,\n1127|<code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>,\n1128|<code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>,\n1129|<code>backend_generation:string[1..256]</code>,\n1130|<code>before_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1131|<code>after_state:TerminalInstanceState</code>,\n1132|<code>side_effects:sorted-unique TerminalBackendSideEffect[0..10]</code>,\n1133|<code>evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]</code>, and\n1134|<code>retry_disposition:replay_same|status_first|new_authorization|required_operator_action</code>.\n1135|Every repeated identity MUST equal the request context.\n1136|\n1137|The ten operation request and success bodies are closed objects containing\n1138|exactly the listed members. <code>Entrypoint</code> is the closed object\n1139|<code>{argv:string[3]}</code>, and its three values MUST be literal\n1140|<code>ax</code>, literal <code>pane</code>, and the canonical request Session\n1141|UUIDv7 string. <code>attach_descriptor</code> is a sensitive opaque\n1142|<code>string[1..4096]</code> usable only on the responding host and MUST NOT be\n1143|persisted or replicated.\n1144|\n1145|| Operation | Exact body input | Exact success result |\n1146|| --- | --- | --- |\n1147|| <code>manifest</code> | <code>{deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{manifest:TerminalBackendManifest}</code> |\n1148|| <code>probe</code> | <code>{platform:macos\\|linux\\|wsl2\\|windows,os_version:string[1..256],requested_capabilities:sorted-unique TerminalBackendCapability[0..16],deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{probe:TerminalBackendProbe,evidence:sorted-by-evidence_id unique CapabilityEvidence[0..256]}</code> |\n1149|| <code>create</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7,entrypoint:Entrypoint,presentation_transport:PresentationTransport,interactive:boolean}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096]\\|null}</code> |\n1150|| <code>attach</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256],client_id:UUIDv7,transport:PresentationTransport,input_authorized:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp,authorization:AttachAuthorization}</code> | <code>{client_mirror_id:UUIDv7,attach_descriptor:string[1..4096],input_authorized:boolean,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[1..256]}</code> |\n1151|| <code>status</code> | <code>{session_id:UUIDv7,terminal_instance_id:UUIDv7\\|null,terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id,implementation_version:semver,protocol_version:semver,backend_generation:string[1..256]\\|null,include_provider_observation:boolean,deadline_at:timestamp}</code> | <code>{state:TerminalInstanceState,identity_match:boolean,wrapper_present:boolean,provider_present:boolean\\|null,attachable:boolean,last_operation_id:UUIDv7\\|null,last_effect:TerminalStatusLastEffect\\|null,evidence_ids:sorted-unique digest[0..256]}</code> |\n1152|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,input_closed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1153|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,quiescence_generation:UUIDv7,provider_proof_kind:ProviderProofKind,timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,observed_at:timestamp}</code> |\n1154|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,safe_boundary_evidence_id:digest,graceful_timeout_ms:uint53[1..3600000]}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,process_closed:true,store_closed:true}</code> |\n1155|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,stale_lease_id:UUIDv4,stale_epoch:uint53[1..9007199254740991],diagnostic_evidence_id:digest}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,target_incarnation_closed:true}</code> |\n1156|| <code>restore</code> | <code>{context:MutationContext,prior_binding_id:digest,checkpoint_id:digest,bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7}</code> | <code>{mutation:MutationResult,binding:TerminalInstanceBinding,restored_parked:true}</code> |\n1157|\n1158|For <code>status</code>, <code>terminal_instance_id</code> and\n1159|<code>backend_generation</code> are either both null (Session-scoped lookup) or\n1160|both non-null (exact-instance lookup). A successful exact-instance result sets\n1161|<code>identity_match</code> true only when Session, instance, backend,\n1162|implementation, protocol, and generation all match. A non-match sets\n1163|<code>identity_match:false</code>, <code>state:absent</code>,\n1164|<code>wrapper_present:false</code>, <code>provider_present:null</code>,\n1165|<code>attachable:false</code>, and both last fields null; it does not authorize\n1166|fallback. <code>provider_present</code> is null unless provider observation was\n1167|requested and evidenced. <code>attachable</code> is true only in\n1168|<code>parked|active</code> with a currently evidenced matching attach\n1169|capability. In <code>attach</code>, the result input boolean MUST equal both the\n1170|request and AttachAuthorization; <code>attach_descriptor</code> in\n1171|<code>create</code> is non-null exactly when <code>interactive</code> is true.\n1172|\n1173|The following table is the exact transition, authorization, idempotency,\n1174|deadline/recovery, evidence, capability, and Structured Error 1.3 mapping.\n1175|An error not listed for an operation MUST NOT be emitted by the backend for a\n1176|syntactically valid request; AX-local parsing may additionally emit\n1177|<code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>. <code>same</code> means no state\n1178|transition and no side effect.\n1179|\n1180|| Operation | Allowed source → success state; exact side effects | Authorization and idempotency key | Deadline/lost-result recovery and required evidence | Capability dependencies | Allowed error codes |\n1181|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1182|| <code>manifest</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | none; byte-stable by executable/implementation digest | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry request; Manifest ID is evidence | none | <code>terminal_backend_protocol_incompatible</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1183|| <code>probe</code> | no Terminal Instance source or target; none | trusted implementation; key is request ID | <code>deadline_at</code> closes adapter; retry with a new request ID; Probe plus evidence for every true claim | none | <code>terminal_backend_untrusted</code>, <code>terminal_backend_manifest_probe_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_implementation_drift</code>, <code>terminal_backend_protocol_error</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1184|| <code>create</code> | <code>absent|stopped</code> → <code>active</code> when interactive, otherwise <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_started</code> and optionally <code>attach_client_created</code> | <code>create</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before <code>wrapper_started</code>; identical retry replays it; uncertainty requires <code>status</code>; binding plus capability/credential evidence | <code>headless_creation</code> when non-interactive; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when provider credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1185|| <code>attach</code> | <code>parked</code> → <code>active</code> or <code>active</code> → <code>active</code>; <code>attach_client_created</code> | valid unexpired AttachAuthorization equal to request transport/input; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/\" + client_id</code> | timeout creates no authorized input unless the durable client receipt says so; retry same client ID; attach-policy/capability evidence | matching <code>local_attach|remote_attach|web_attach</code>; <code>multi_attach</code> for overlap; <code>multiple_input_clients</code> plus AX policy for concurrent input | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1186|| <code>status</code> | <code>absent|creating|parked|active|quiescing|stopped|stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → same state; none | none; key is full queried identity tuple | timeout/read failure is unknown, never absent; retry query; status evidence IDs only | <code>provider_process_observation</code> exactly when provider observation requested | <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1187|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>active|parked</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>input_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/quiesce/\" + quiescence_generation</code> | receipt precedes input closure; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; evidence binds closure time/generation | <code>input_quiescence</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1188|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>quiescing</code>; <code>safe_boundary_observed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/boundary/\" + quiescence_generation + \"/\" + provider_proof_kind</code> | lesser of request deadline and timeout; identical retry returns the same proof; no proof on timeout; safe-boundary evidence | <code>safe_boundary_observation</code>; also <code>provider_process_observation</code> for provider proof kinds | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>quiesce_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1189|| <code>request-stop</code> | <code>quiescing</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>graceful_stop_requested,process_closed,backend_store_closed</code> | <code>control</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/stop/\" + safe_boundary_evidence_id</code> | lesser deadline/timeout; lost result requires <code>status</code>, then same-key retry only if not closed; boundary and closure evidence | <code>graceful_stop</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>stop_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1190|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>stale_fenced|unavailable</code> → <code>stopped</code>; <code>stale_incarnation_terminated,process_closed</code> | <code>force_stale</code>; UTF-8 <code>terminal_instance_id + \"/terminate/\" + stale_lease_id + \"/\" + decimal(stale_epoch)</code> | deadline may leave uncertain closure; use <code>status</code> before same-key retry; diagnostic, fencing, and closure evidence | <code>stale_process_termination</code> and <code>provider_process_observation</code> | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1191|| <code>restore</code> | <code>absent|stopped|unavailable</code> → <code>parked</code>; <code>binding_persisted,wrapper_restored</code> | <code>restore</code>; UTF-8 <code>session_id + \"/\" + bootstrap_operation_id</code> | persist receipt before restore; identical retry replays; uncertainty uses <code>status</code>; prior binding, Checkpoint, new binding, capability/credential evidence | <code>reboot_restoration</code>; <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> when credentials are required | <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>, <code>local_precondition_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unauthorized</code>, <code>terminal_backend_stale_generation</code>, <code>terminal_backend_capability_unproven</code>, <code>terminal_backend_restore_mismatch</code>, <code>terminal_backend_unavailable</code>, <code>terminal_backend_timeout</code>, <code>terminal_backend_process_failed</code>, <code>terminal_backend_integrity_failure</code> |\n1192|\n1193|Create is idempotent on <code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code> across\n1194|controller crash and lost result. AX and backend durably bind the pair before\n1195|the first child side effect. Identical retry returns the one result/instance;\n1196|a changed operation in the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>.\n1197|Only a successful status read proves absence. Attach is ownership-observational\n1198|for current-owner resume, local/remote/web, reconnect, and multi-attach.\n1199|\n1200|### 4.D Closed capabilities and evidence\n1201|\n1202|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapability</dfn> is the exact 16-value registry below.\n1203|<dfn>TerminalBackendOperation</dfn> is exactly\n1204|<code>manifest|probe|create|attach|status|quiesce-input|wait-safe-boundary|request-stop|terminate-stale|restore</code>.\n1205|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceRequirement</dfn> is exactly\n1206|<code>conformance_fixture|runtime_probe|credential_sentinel|provider_auth_smoke|policy_authorization</code>.\n1207|\n1208|<dfn>TerminalBackendCapabilityClaim</dfn> is a closed object containing exactly\n1209|<code>capability:TerminalBackendCapability</code>,\n1210|<code>origin:static|probed</code>, <code>value:boolean</code>,\n1211|<code>generation_variable:boolean</code>,\n1212|<code>dependent_operations:sorted-unique TerminalBackendOperation[1..10]</code>,\n1213|and <code>evidence_requirements:sorted-unique CapabilityEvidenceRequirement[1..5]</code>.\n1214|The latter three members MUST exactly equal the registry row for the capability;\n1215|a Manifest or Probe cannot redefine them. A false claim is retained to make a\n1216|probed refusal explicit but confers no operation.\n1217|\n1218|| Capability | Exact semantics | Generation-variable | Exact dependent operations | Exact evidence requirements |\n1219|| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1220|| <code>durable_disconnect</code> | Wrapper survives every client disconnect. | false | <code>create,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1221|| <code>local_attach</code> | Local-only presentation. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1222|| <code>remote_attach</code> | Presentation over trusted private mesh only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1223|| <code>web_attach</code> | Web presentation over an admitted transport only. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1224|| <code>multi_attach</code> | Concurrent presentation clients; no multi-input or ownership implication. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1225|| <code>headless_creation</code> | Create without UI or prompt in the proven execution realm. | true | <code>create</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1226|| <code>reboot_restoration</code> | Re-establish after reboot; does not claim process survival. | true | <code>restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1227|| <code>input_quiescence</code> | Reject new input with generation-bound evidence. | true | <code>quiesce-input</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1228|| <code>safe_boundary_observation</code> | Observe AX/provider-selected safe-boundary proof. | true | <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1229|| <code>provider_process_observation</code> | Observe provider presence without PID identity. | true | <code>status,terminate-stale,wait-safe-boundary</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1230|| <code>graceful_stop</code> | Request and observe orderly exit. | true | <code>request-stop</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1231|| <code>stale_process_termination</code> | Target one fenced stale incarnation. | true | <code>terminate-stale</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1232|| <code>terminal_state_retention</code> | Retain local presentation state, never portable Checkpoint state. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1233|| <code>scrollback_retention</code> | Retain local scrollback, never replicated terminal output. | true | <code>create,restore,status</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,runtime_probe</code> |\n1234|| <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> | Exact instance passes AX sentinel and provider-auth smoke without UI. | true | <code>create,restore</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,credential_sentinel,provider_auth_smoke,runtime_probe</code> |\n1235|| <code>multiple_input_clients</code> | Backend serializes multiple input clients; AX policy separately authorizes use. | true | <code>attach</code> | <code>conformance_fixture,policy_authorization,runtime_probe</code> |\n1236|\n1237|<dfn>CapabilityEvidenceFact</dfn> is the exact enum\n1238|<code>fixture_passed|runtime_probe_passed|sentinel_passed|provider_auth_passed|policy_checked|ui_absent|prompt_absent</code>.\n1239|Capability Evidence 1.0.0 is the following closed immutable object; no other\n1240|member is permitted:\n1241|\n1242|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n1243|| --- | --- |\n1244|| <code>schema</code> | literal <code>urn:ax:schema:terminal-capability-evidence</code> |\n1245|| <code>schema_version</code> | literal <code>1.0.0</code> |\n1246|| <code>evidence_id</code> | digest computed by the Section 4.B identity rule |\n1247|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | terminal-backend-id |\n1248|| <code>implementation_version</code> | semver equal to Manifest and Probe |\n1249|| <code>protocol_version</code> | semver equal to Probe |\n1250|| <code>backend_generation_digest</code> | digest equal to Probe |\n1251|| <code>capability</code> | TerminalBackendCapability |\n1252|| <code>value</code> | literal <code>true</code> |\n1253|| <code>platform</code> | <code>macos|linux|wsl2|windows</code> equal to Probe |\n1254|| <code>os_version</code> | string[1..256] equal to Probe |\n1255|| <code>conformance_fixture_id</code> | digest equal to Manifest |\n1256|| <code>observed_at</code> | timestamp |\n1257|| <code>expires_at</code> | timestamp strictly after <code>observed_at</code> |\n1258|| <code>issuer</code> | <code>ax_release|ax_local_probe</code> |\n1259|| <code>issuer_id</code> | digest of the AX release signing identity for <code>ax_release</code>, or digest of the host-incarnation identity for <code>ax_local_probe</code> |\n1260|| <code>attestation_signature</code> | <code>rsa-sha256:</code> plus Base64 RFC 4648 signature by the trusted <code>issuer_id</code> key over the domain-separated JCS object with <code>evidence_id</code> and this member omitted |\n1261|| <code>facts</code> | sorted unique CapabilityEvidenceFact[1..7] |\n1262|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1263|| <code>provider_id</code> | provider-id|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1264|| <code>provider_build</code> | string[1..256]|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1265|| <code>sentinel_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1266|| <code>provider_auth_smoke_result</code> | literal <code>passed</code>|null; required only for <code>credential_capable_execution_realm</code> and null otherwise |\n1267|| <code>extensions</code> | exact empty object <code>{}</code> |\n1268|\n1269|Credential-realm evidence binds the opaque Terminal Instance Binding digest,\n1270|AX-owned sentinel result, provider ID/build, and provider-auth smoke result. It\n1271|contains neither the Terminal Instance ID nor raw generation.\n1272|The signed bytes are ASCII <code>ax-terminal-capability-evidence-v1</code>, one\n1273|zero byte, and the Section 1.6 canonical bytes of the evidence object after\n1274|omitting exactly <code>evidence_id</code> and <code>attestation_signature</code>.\n1275|AX resolves <code>issuer_id</code> through its trusted release/host-incarnation\n1276|key registry and MUST verify the signature before treating the object as\n1277|evidence; a caller-supplied issuer ID is not authentication. Missing, malformed,\n1278|unknown-key, or invalid signatures fail closed before capability admission.\n1279|GUI/Aqua bootstrap alone is not proof. Missing, expired, self-minted,\n1280|contradictory, or wrong-generation evidence disables the claim. Static claims\n1281|never override a failed probe; generation-variable claims re-probe on generation\n1282|change and before activation.\n1283|\n1284|Multi/remote/web attach never implies multiple authorized input sources or\n1285|ownership. Multi-input is separately declared and policy-gated. Restore/resume\n1286|MUST NOT silently fall back to another backend; defaults apply only to new\n1287|activation when policy allows.\n1288|\n1289|### 4.E Persistence, transport, security, and compatibility\n1290|\n1291|| Classification | Members and rule |\n1292|| --- | --- |\n1293|| Safe immutable evidence | Sanitized backend identity/version/platform/conformance/capability evidence; MAY persist and replicate after validation. |\n1294|| Host-local durable metadata | Instance/binding IDs, sanitized native reference, generation, idempotency receipt, last effect; host-local, non-replicable. |\n1295|| Derived cache | Discovery/availability/attachability/process observations and probe views; rebuildable, non-authoritative. |\n1296|| Sensitive runtime state | IPC, tmux sockets, named pipes, attach/relay credentials, backend auth/live databases, GUI/login attestations, provider credentials; owner-only and non-replicable. |\n1297|| Forbidden | Raw native reference, PID/handle, endpoint/token, terminal output/scrollback, unrestricted environment, credential detail, and live-process facts MUST NOT replicate. |\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
