{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c509","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":223,"recorded_at":1780531400000441,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-f8fd-7c80-a831-0f1c1c4c63c1"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-f8fd-7c80-a831-0f1c1c4c63c1","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01d-f8fd-7c80-a831-0f1c1c4c63c1","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1769 line(s) above)\n1770|<code>session.stopped</code>, <code>session.resumed</code>,\n1771|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>,\n1772|<code>lease.transferred</code>, <code>lease.forced</code>,\n1773|<code>session.parked</code>, <code>session.failed</code>,\n1774|<code>fork.created</code>, <code>profile.changed</code>,\n1775|<code>session.tombstoned</code>, <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>,\n1776|<code>replica.replace_confirmed</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n1777|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, <code>tombstone.issued</code>, and\n1778|<code>tombstone.resolved</code>.\n1779|\n1780|The <code>payload</code> object is a closed tagged union selected by\n1781|<code>event_type</code>. It MUST contain exactly the members in this table; a\n1782|member shown as nullable remains required:\n1783|\n1784|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1785|| --- | --- |\n1786|| <code>session.created</code> | <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>first_checkpoint_operation_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n1787|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1788|| <code>provider.launched</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code> |\n1789|| <code>provider.identified</code> | <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak</code> |\n1790|| <code>session.idle</code> | <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code> |\n1791|| <code>session.quiescing</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>reason:graceful_takeover&#124;stop&#124;checkpoint</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code> |\n1792|| <code>checkpoint.created</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>kind:periodic&#124;pre_stop&#124;closure&#124;fork_base&#124;manual</code> |\n1793|| <code>sync.completed</code> | <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>materialized:boolean</code> |\n1794|| <code>session.stopped</code> | <code>graceful:boolean</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>resumable:boolean</code>, <code>closure_kind:checkpointed&#124;bootstrap_abort</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code> |\n1795|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1796|| <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>failure_phase:before_terminal&#124;after_terminal&#124;after_process&#124;after_identity&#124;before_checkpoint</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>resume_allowed:false</code> |\n1797|| <code>lease.transferred</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>from_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>to_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>predecessor_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1798|| <code>lease.forced</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n1799|| <code>session.parked</code> | <code>reason:remote_owner&#124;stale_owner&#124;restore_policy&#124;failed_handoff</code>, <code>winning_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1800|| <code>session.failed</code> | <code>error_code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>retryable:boolean</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n1801|| <code>fork.created</code> | <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>new_session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>source_profile_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1802|| <code>profile.changed</code> | <code>from:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>to:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>confirmed:boolean</code> |\n1803|| <code>session.tombstoned</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code> |\n1804|| <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>accepted_risks:sorted unique enum[3]</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1805|| <code>replica.replace_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_marker_id:digest</code>, <code>expected_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>replacement_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1806|| <code>task_board.launched</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code>, <code>state:running&#124;idle</code> |\n1807|| <code>task_board.adopted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:digest</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code> |\n1808|| <code>tombstone.issued</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>scope:session&#124;workspace_entry&#124;provider_snapshot&#124;managed_replica</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code> |\n1809|| <code>tombstone.resolved</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>resolution:deleted&#124;already_absent&#124;resurrected&#124;retained_conflict</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>resulting_entry_digest:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1810|\n1811|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1812|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1813|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1814|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1815|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1816|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1817|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1818|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1819|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1820|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1821|null.\n1822|\n1823|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1824|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1825|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1826|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1827|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1828|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1829|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1830|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1831|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1832|\n1833|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1834|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1835|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1836|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1837|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1838|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1839|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1840|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1841|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1842|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1843|\n1844|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1845|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1846|\n1847|Normative example:\n1848|\n1849|~~~json\n1850|{\n1851|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1852|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1853|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1854|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1855|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1856|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1857|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1858|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1859|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1860|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1861|  \"predecessors\": [\n1862|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1863|  ],\n1864|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1865|  \"payload\": {\n1866|    \"graceful\": true,\n1867|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1868|    \"resumable\": true,\n1869|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c50b","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":224,"recorded_at":1780531400000443,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01d-f8fd-7c80-a831-0f1c1c4c63c1"},"task_id":"01a0b01d-f8fd-7c80-a831-0f1c1c4c63c1","event":{"kind":"completed","task_id":"01a0b01d-f8fd-7c80-a831-0f1c1c4c63c1"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c50d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":225,"recorded_at":1780531400000445,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01df1c1777d86548290a32f9b8d","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1339 line(s) above)\n1340|shapes.\n1341|\n1342|**Future candidate (non-normative; unavailable): Superlogical.** Dated public\n1343|sources retrieved 2026-08-29 describe planned reconnect/share, web/native\n1344|clients, software-driven structured actions, and libghostty use; the official\n1345|GitHub organization exposed no public repositories that day. They establish no\n1346|public release, AX adapter, API/SDK/protocol, backend ID/version, capability\n1347|evidence, lifecycle, ownership, security, or replication contract. The label\n1348|enables nothing. Admission requires dated evidence for create, attach/reconnect,\n1349|status/generation, quiescence, graceful/stale stop, restore, exact\n1350|<code>ax pane</code>, headless automation, credential proof, transport/auth,\n1351|no AX ownership/authoritative-state transfer, and crash/security/conformance\n1352|negative tests.\n1353|\n1354|### 4.1 Terminal backend interface\n1355|\n1356|Every terminal backend MUST implement these semantic operations:\n1357|\n1358|| Operation | Required result |\n1359|| --- | --- |\n1360|| <code>create</code> | With <code>session_id</code> and caller-stable <code>bootstrap_operation_id</code>, create a durable pane/process whose only stable entry point is <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>. |\n1361|| <code>attach</code> | Connect an operator to the local terminal without changing ownership. |\n1362|| <code>status</code> | Report process presence, wrapper state, provider child state, and attachability. |\n1363|| <code>quiesce-input</code> | Stop new operator/provider input while retaining observation. |\n1364|| <code>wait-safe-boundary</code> | Prove the adapter-specific safe boundary or time out. |\n1365|| <code>request-stop</code> | Ask the provider to exit through a version-tested graceful path. |\n1366|| <code>terminate-stale</code> | Terminate a process only for explicit force recovery after preserving diagnostics. |\n1367|| <code>restore</code> | Recreate the wrapper after reboot and consult current ownership before any provider resume. |\n1368|\n1369|The wrapper MUST validate configuration, load the logical session, synchronize\n1370|known lease records when possible, and compare the local fencing token before\n1371|launching a provider. It MUST park safely when ownership is remote, ambiguous,\n1372|or unverified.\n1373|\n1374|Terminal creation and the wrapper's first child start are idempotent on\n1375|<code>(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)</code>. The backend MUST durably bind\n1376|that pair before child creation. An identical retry returns or reattaches to\n1377|the one recorded wrapper/child; changing the operation for a session still in\n1378|the bootstrap window is <code>idempotency_mismatch</code>. After a lost result,\n1379|<code>status</code> plus that binding MUST prove absence or identify the one\n1380|child before any start retry. This contract never persists or replicates a PID\n1381|as identity.\n1382|\n1383|### 4.2 tmux backend\n1384|\n1385|On macOS, Linux, and WSL2, the supported durable terminal backend is tmux. Every\n1386|managed pane MUST run:\n1387|\n1388|~~~shell\n1389|ax pane <logical-session-id>\n1390|~~~\n1391|\n1392|It MUST NOT run the raw provider command as the pane's stable command.\n1393|<code>tmux-resurrect</code> plus <code>tmux-continuum</code> MAY recreate local\n1394|tmux layout and invoke the wrapper after reboot. They MUST NOT be described or\n1395|used as cross-host migration.\n1396|\n1397|AX MUST use its dedicated <code>-S</code> server and MUST NOT discover or reuse\n1398|the operator's default tmux server by ambient socket name. On macOS, server\n1399|creation is credential-sensitive. A Background caller MUST NOT create a\n1400|credential-dependent tmux server. A background CLI, SSH RPC process, daemon,\n1401|or restore worker MAY contact an already-running authenticated Aqua broker and\n1402|its attested AX tmux server; if neither exists it MUST return\n1403|<code>capability_unavailable</code> with typed realm/readiness details and MUST\n1404|NOT fall back to direct server creation.\n1405|\n1406|<code>launchctl managername</code> is a diagnostic hint only. Conformance\n1407|requires a functional AX sentinel inside the exact tmux server plus a separate\n1408|provider-auth smoke using the selected provider. Evidence MUST bind the exact\n1409|tmux server generation, provider build, and macOS version. Aqua alone and\n1410|sentinel-only evidence are insufficient. Any provider flow requiring GUI\n1411|interaction, Keychain UI, a permission prompt, or other human action fails\n1412|closed until that interaction succeeds in the verified GUI realm.\n1413|\n1414|After restore, the wrapper MUST:\n1415|\n1416|1. read the latest locally known lease;\n1417|2. attempt a mesh lease refresh without blocking forever;\n1418|3. resume locally only if the local host has the winning lease and the required\n1419|   materialization is valid;\n1420|4. offer remote attach/takeover when another host owns the session in an\n1421|   interactive terminal; or\n1422|5. enter <code>parked</code> without launching the provider in all other cases.\n1423|\n1424|Logout or reboot invalidates unrenewed realm evidence. Without a verified GUI\n1425|realm, recovery MUST remain parked until GUI login re-establishes the broker,\n1426|functional sentinel, provider-auth smoke, and their generation/build/version\n1427|binding. A cached sentinel or prior <code>managername</code> observation MUST\n1428|NOT authorize resume.\n1429|\n1430|### 4.3 Native Windows backend\n1431|\n1432|Native Windows PowerShell MUST use a Windows terminal backend implemented with\n1433|Go process supervision and ConPTY. It MUST support mesh sync, workspace and\n1434|provider materialization, direct/provider resume, task-board open/adopt, remote\n1435|attach, graceful takeover when the provider row passes ConPTY gates, force\n1436|takeover, stop, and continuation.\n1437|\n1438|Native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux or tmux resurrection. A reboot destroys the\n1439|live ConPTY. The user service MUST recreate <code>ax pane SESSION_ID</code>,\n1440|which resumes from the latest valid checkpoint only after lease validation.\n1441|Terminal scrollback and live process memory are not portable state.\n1442|\n1443|Full tmux restore on a Windows computer is a WSL2 feature and uses the Linux\n1444|paths, process model, and provider installation inside that distribution. A\n1445|native Windows provider store and a WSL2 provider store are distinct\n1446|materialization targets.\n1447|\n1448|### 4.4 User services\n1449|\n1450|The background service integration is:\n1451|\n1452|- a launchd agent on macOS;\n1453|- a systemd user unit on Linux and WSL2 where systemd is enabled;\n1454|- otherwise an explicitly installed per-user periodic launcher on WSL2; and\n1455|- a Scheduled Task or per-user service on native Windows.\n1456|\n1457|The service MAY run periodic sync, peer health checks, tombstone\n1458|acknowledgement, stale-process detection, and wrapper restoration. Core commands\n1459|MUST work without it. Service absence MUST degrade freshness, not corrupt\n1460|ownership.\n1461|\n1462|The macOS launchd background control plane and Aqua terminal broker are separate\n1463|roles. The control plane MUST NOT acquire GUI/Keychain authority by proxy and\n1464|MUST NOT create a credential-dependent tmux server. The Aqua broker exposes\n1465|only authenticated, same-user, generation-bound terminal readiness and server\n1466|operations; it does not gain lease, workspace, provider, or replication\n1467|authority.\n1468|\n1469|## 5. Domain records and state machine\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c50f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":226,"recorded_at":1780531400000447,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"call_id":"call_01a0b01df52d7068a4617b0409211ba0","text":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1769 line(s) above)\n1770|<code>session.stopped</code>, <code>session.resumed</code>,\n1771|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code>,\n1772|<code>lease.transferred</code>, <code>lease.forced</code>,\n1773|<code>session.parked</code>, <code>session.failed</code>,\n1774|<code>fork.created</code>, <code>profile.changed</code>,\n1775|<code>session.tombstoned</code>, <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>,\n1776|<code>replica.replace_confirmed</code>, <code>task_board.launched</code>,\n1777|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, <code>tombstone.issued</code>, and\n1778|<code>tombstone.resolved</code>.\n1779|\n1780|The <code>payload</code> object is a closed tagged union selected by\n1781|<code>event_type</code>. It MUST contain exactly the members in this table; a\n1782|member shown as nullable remains required:\n1783|\n1784|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1785|| --- | --- |\n1786|| <code>session.created</code> | <code>session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>bootstrap_operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>first_checkpoint_operation_id:UUIDv7</code> |\n1787|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>terminal_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1788|| <code>provider.launched</code> | <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>provider_version:string[1..128]</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>profile_mapping:string[1..512]</code> |\n1789|| <code>provider.identified</code> | <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest</code>, <code>confidence:exact&#124;strong&#124;weak</code> |\n1790|| <code>session.idle</code> | <code>boundary_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>foreground_idle:boolean</code>, <code>background_idle:boolean</code> |\n1791|| <code>session.quiescing</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>reason:graceful_takeover&#124;stop&#124;checkpoint</code>, <code>input_blocked:boolean</code> |\n1792|| <code>checkpoint.created</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>kind:periodic&#124;pre_stop&#124;closure&#124;fork_base&#124;manual</code> |\n1793|| <code>sync.completed</code> | <code>peer_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>manifest_ids:sorted unique digest[1..1024]</code>, <code>materialized:boolean</code> |\n1794|| <code>session.stopped</code> | <code>graceful:boolean</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>resumable:boolean</code>, <code>closure_kind:checkpointed&#124;bootstrap_abort</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code> |\n1795|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_backend:tmux&#124;conpty</code>, <code>native_session_id:string[1..512]</code> |\n1796|| <code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>failure_phase:before_terminal&#124;after_terminal&#124;after_process&#124;after_identity&#124;before_checkpoint</code>, <code>provider_identity_record_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]&#124;null</code>, <code>process_closed:boolean</code>, <code>store_closed:boolean</code>, <code>resume_allowed:false</code> |\n1797|| <code>lease.transferred</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>from_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>to_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>predecessor_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1798|| <code>lease.forced</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>new_lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code> |\n1799|| <code>session.parked</code> | <code>reason:remote_owner&#124;stale_owner&#124;restore_policy&#124;failed_handoff</code>, <code>winning_lease_id:UUIDv4</code> |\n1800|| <code>session.failed</code> | <code>error_code:string[1..128]</code>, <code>retryable:boolean</code>, <code>operation_id:UUIDv7&#124;null</code> |\n1801|| <code>fork.created</code> | <code>source_session_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>source_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>new_session_record_id:digest</code>, <code>provider_fork_mode:native&#124;supported_import&#124;task_board_clone</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>source_profile_event_id:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1802|| <code>profile.changed</code> | <code>from:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>to:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>confirmed:boolean</code> |\n1803|| <code>session.tombstoned</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code> |\n1804|| <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_owner_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_epoch:uint53</code>, <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>accepted_risks:sorted unique enum[3]</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1805|| <code>replica.replace_confirmed</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>workspace_group_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_host_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>managed_replica_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>expected_marker_id:digest</code>, <code>expected_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>replacement_checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>confirmation_mode:interactive&#124;non_interactive</code> |\n1806|| <code>task_board.launched</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>provider_id:provider-id</code>, <code>launch_mode:primary_owner&#124;tracked_prompt</code>, <code>lease_epoch:uint53&gt;0</code>, <code>lease_id:UUIDv4</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code>, <code>state:running&#124;idle</code> |\n1807|| <code>task_board.adopted</code> | <code>operation_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>bundle_id:digest</code>, <code>manager_session_ref:string[1..512]</code>, <code>board_goal_id:string[1..128]&#124;null</code>, <code>board_goal_revision:uint53&#124;null</code> |\n1808|| <code>tombstone.issued</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>scope:session&#124;workspace_entry&#124;provider_snapshot&#124;managed_replica</code>, <code>subject_id:UUIDv7</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code> |\n1809|| <code>tombstone.resolved</code> | <code>tombstone_id:digest</code>, <code>resolution:deleted&#124;already_absent&#124;resurrected&#124;retained_conflict</code>, <code>target_ref:string[1..1024]</code>, <code>resulting_entry_digest:digest&#124;null</code> |\n1810|\n1811|For <code>takeover.force_confirmed</code>, <code>accepted_risks</code> MUST be\n1812|exactly <code>[\"divergent_history\",\"split_brain\",\"stale_process\"]</code> in\n1813|bytewise order. For <code>task_board.launched</code> and\n1814|<code>task_board.adopted</code>, goal ID and revision MUST\n1815|either both be null or both be non-null, and a non-null revision is greater\n1816|than zero. A <code>task_board.launched</code> event MUST repeat the winning\n1817|creation lease and the Session Record's provider/launch mode; a mismatch is\n1818|<code>integrity_failure</code>. Audit event issuance and retention are specified\n1819|in Sections 10.7 and 18.4. A <code>tombstone.resolved</code> resurrection\n1820|requires a non-null resulting entry digest; every other resolution requires\n1821|null.\n1822|\n1823|The profile and profile-source pair in every launch, resume, and fork event\n1824|MUST equal the Section 2.4 effective profile at the referenced checkpoint or,\n1825|for the first launch, the Session Record and null. A non-null source MUST name\n1826|the newest authoritative <code>profile.changed</code> event in that event-head\n1827|closure. Equal provider mapping strings do not permit changing either value.\n1828|For <code>fork.created</code>, the effective new-session authority is its newly\n1829|persisted Session Record, so <code>profile_source_event_id</code> is null.\n1830|<code>source_profile_event_id</code> separately equals the nullable source-\n1831|checkpoint profile event and never participates in new-session derivation.\n1832|\n1833|A <code>session.stopped</code> payload is <code>checkpointed</code> exactly when\n1834|<code>checkpoint_id</code> is non-null and <code>resumable = true</code>.\n1835|<code>bootstrap_abort</code> requires a null checkpoint, false resumable and\n1836|graceful values, and a preceding or equal-operation\n1837|<code>session.bootstrap_aborted</code> event; its derived lifecycle is\n1838|<code>failed</code>, never <code>stopped</code>. A bootstrap-aborted event\n1839|requires both closure booleans true. Its identity fields are both null before\n1840|identity, and after identity exactly the field belonging to the Session Record\n1841|kind is non-null. An ambiguous live process or open store cannot be represented\n1842|as a successful abort and remains <code>failed</code> with recovery diagnostics.\n1843|\n1844|An unknown event type MUST be retained as an immutable object but MUST NOT\n1845|change derived session state under major version 1.\n1846|\n1847|Normative example:\n1848|\n1849|~~~json\n1850|{\n1851|  \"schema\": \"urn:ax:schema:session-event\",\n1852|  \"schema_version\": \"1.0.0\",\n1853|  \"event_id\": \"sha256:46d2745fe7dfce856027be36e34f1cc6a56ffc846063dc4aa6aabf3f5a85bacb\",\n1854|  \"subject_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1855|  \"session_id\": \"0198f4c8-3e70-7a11-8a2b-1234567890ab\",\n1856|  \"event_type\": \"session.stopped\",\n1857|  \"created_by_host_id\": \"0198f4c8-4a10-7b22-8b3c-1234567890ab\",\n1858|  \"lease_epoch\": 4,\n1859|  \"lease_id\": \"aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee\",\n1860|  \"lease_sequence\": 12,\n1861|  \"predecessors\": [\n1862|    \"sha256:7777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777777\"\n1863|  ],\n1864|  \"created_at\": \"2026-08-19T04:08:00.000Z\",\n1865|  \"payload\": {\n1866|    \"graceful\": true,\n1867|    \"checkpoint_id\": \"sha256:e051996f51f13ace4f5cdebe1e30fd26fd5fe104cfd6e6a7f9f1206ba3819656\",\n1868|    \"resumable\": true,\n1869|    \"closure_kind\": \"checkpointed\",\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
