{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c53f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":250,"recorded_at":1780531400000495,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01e-09d3-7da3-ad00-db2461b4dff3"},"task_id":"01a0b01e-09d3-7da3-ad00-db2461b4dff3","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"01a0b01e-09d3-7da3-ad00-db2461b4dff3","span_id":"c120b06e01a1cc90"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c541","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":251,"recorded_at":1780531400000497,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01e-09b2-7bc1-9aea-b108affa9e75"},"task_id":"01a0b01e-09b2-7bc1-9aea-b108affa9e75","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01e-09b2-7bc1-9aea-b108affa9e75","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(1876 line(s) above)\n1877|#### Session Event 4.0.0 Terminal Instance events\n1878|\n1879|Session Event 4.0.0 retains the exact v3 top-level closed shape, digest rules,\n1880|lease ordering, predecessor rules, and complete v1-v3 event-type registry. It\n1881|changes exactly the payload definitions for <code>terminal.created</code> and\n1882|<code>session.resumed</code>; every other v1-v3 payload remains byte-for-byte\n1883|the definition selected by v3. The two v4 payloads are:\n1884|\n1885|| Event type | Exact payload members |\n1886|| --- | --- |\n1887|| <code>terminal.created</code> | <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1888|| <code>session.resumed</code> | <code>checkpoint_id:digest</code>, <code>execution_profile:standard&#124;yolo</code>, <code>profile_source_event_id:digest&#124;null</code>, <code>terminal_binding_id:digest</code>, <code>terminal_backend_id:terminal-backend-id</code>, <code>implementation_version:semver</code>, <code>protocol_version:semver</code>, <code>evidence_ids:sorted unique digest[1..256]</code> |\n1889|\n1890|The binding digest is an opaque audit reference to a host-local Terminal\n1891|Instance Binding; the binding object itself is not an event member and is not\n1892|replicated. The evidence IDs MUST resolve locally to validated, sanitized\n1893|Manifest, Probe, and applicable Capability Evidence objects bound to the event's\n1894|backend ID and versions. They MUST NOT resolve through the event to a native\n1895|reference, generation string, socket, pipe, endpoint, token, credential,\n1896|terminal output, PID/handle, or live-process fact.\n1897|\n1898|<code>terminal.created</code> records the backend selected for a new AX-\n1899|authorized activation. <code>session.resumed</code> records the backend used by\n1900|that owner resume. A valid takeover or owner resume MAY select a different\n1901|admitted destination backend and emits a new binding digest and v4 event; it\n1902|does not clone/fork the LogicalSession and never mutates an earlier event.\n1903|Attach or presentation-client activity emits neither event and cannot change\n1904|Owner/Replica, lease, or fencing state. A reader of v1-v3 may retain a v4 event\n1905|as inert immutable history but MUST NOT derive runtime state or write a lower-\n1906|version replacement.\n1907|\n1908|### 5.3 Lease Record and ownership\n1909|\n1910|The Lease Record schema is <code>urn:ax:schema:lease</code> version\n1911|<code>1.0.0</code>. Fields are:\n1912|\n1913|| Field | Type | Constraint |\n1914|| --- | --- | --- |\n1915|| <code>schema</code> | string | Exact Lease Record schema identifier |\n1916|| <code>schema_version</code> | semver | Exact <code>1.0.0</code> |\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
