{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c545","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":253,"recorded_at":1780531400000501,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01e-09d3-7da3-ad00-db2461b4dff3"},"task_id":"01a0b01e-09d3-7da3-ad00-db2461b4dff3","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01e-09d3-7da3-ad00-db2461b4dff3","chunk":"Read text file `internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md`.\n(3517 line(s) above)\n3518|### 7.A Provider Protocol 3.0.0 Terminal Instance binding\n3519|\n3520|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 retains the exact v2 framing, request/result envelopes,\n3521|operation registry, idempotency rules, Provider authority, and embedded types,\n3522|except that every occurrence of the v2 <code>TerminalDescriptor</code> is\n3523|replaced by the following closed v3 object:\n3524|\n3525|| Member | Exact type and constraint |\n3526|| --- | --- |\n3527|| <code>terminal_binding_id</code> | digest of the validated Terminal Instance Binding 1.0.0 |\n3528|| <code>terminal_instance_id</code> | AX-assigned UUIDv7; never a PID, socket, path, pipe, URL, handle, token, or native reference |\n3529|| <code>terminal_backend_id</code> | Section 4.B registered backend ID |\n3530|| <code>implementation_version</code> | Semantic Version equal to the admitted Manifest and Probe |\n3531|| <code>protocol_version</code> | Semantic Version in Terminal Backend Protocol major 1 |\n3532|| <code>backend_generation</code> | string[1..256] equal to the host-local binding generation; lengths 0 and 257 are invalid |\n3533|| <code>interactive</code> | boolean |\n3534|| <code>columns</code> / <code>rows</code> | uint16[1..1000] |\n3535|\n3536|No other member is permitted. The descriptor is AX-supplied delegated process-\n3537|hosting context; it conveys no Session ownership, lease, provider identity,\n3538|workspace, checkpoint, replication, or takeover authority to the Provider or\n3539|TerminalBackend. The Provider MUST reject a descriptor whose binding digest,\n3540|backend ID/version, or generation does not match the AX-validated host-local\n3541|binding before launching or observing a provider process. The provider still\n3542|receives the LeaseToken separately and MUST apply its v2 fencing rules.\n3543|\n3544|Provider Protocol 3.0.0 binds Structured Error 1.3.0. A syntactically valid v3\n3545|request receives the v3 envelope with Error 1.3 on failure. A v2/v3 major\n3546|mismatch, an unparseable or oversize first frame, or output that cannot be\n3547|framed follows the Section 15.1 close/termination rule; the caller never trusts\n3548|a different major's error. A dual-stack adapter advertises and validates v2 and\n3549|v3 independently. It MAY translate only <code>ax.tmux</code> and\n3550|<code>ax.conpty</code> to the immutable v2 descriptor under Section 4.E; every\n3551|other backend is <code>incompatible_protocol</code>, not a fallback.\n3552|\n3553|### 7.8 Companion Session Adapter protocol\n3554|\n3555|Cross-environment cloning uses <code>urn:ax:protocol:session-adapter</code>\n3556|1.0.0 in the same trusted <code>ax-provider-&lt;id&gt;</code> executable and with\n3557|the same host-observed executable digest as Provider Protocol 2.0.0. It is not\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
