{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c6d7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":454,"recorded_at":1780531400000903,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b01e-c54a-7432-b406-7022c6c7017e"},"task_id":"01a0b01e-c54a-7432-b406-7022c6c7017e","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b01e-c54a-7432-b406-7022c6c7017e","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-16-1\",\n  \"command\": \"ls .github/workflows/ 2>/dev/null && head -100 .github/workflows/*.y*ml 2>/dev/null | head -120; echo =====; grep -n \\\"axpane\\\\|validation suite\\\\|26-command\\\" README.md | head; echo =====; grep -rn \\\"cataloggen -adopted\\\" --include=\\\"*.md\\\" --include=\\\"*.yml\\\" --include=\\\"*.yaml\\\" --include=\\\"*.json\\\" . 2>/dev/null | grep -v node_modules | head -5\",\n  \"description\": \"Find CI validation suite commands\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"scan_scope_hint\": \"[hint] unscoped recursive scan over the workspace root — scope the next search to the subtree the task names or use the bounded search tool; if this scan backgrounded, harvest or terminate it before ending the turn.\",\n  \"output\": \"ci.yml\\nname: CI\\n\\non:\\n  pull_request:\\n  push:\\n    branches:\\n      - main\\n\\npermissions:\\n  contents: read\\n\\n# What green means. Every job below proves its selection matched something:\\n# a grep, glob, file scan, matrix expansion, or test selector that finds\\n# nothing fails closed instead of passing on an empty result set. No job\\n# declares an `if:` condition, so no job can skip quietly; gates-verdict\\n# additionally refuses any skipped, failed, or cancelled dependency.\\n#\\n# GOOS=windows work is compile-and-vet only. A green windows-compile-only job\\n# proves the tree type-checks for Windows; it never implies executed\\n# behaviour. Coverage is reported as numbers, not enforced as a floor.\\njobs:\\n  contract-preservation:\\n    name: Contract preservation (v0.5.0 current, v0.4.3 historical)\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n    timeout-minutes: 10\\n    steps:\\n      - name: Check out repository\\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\\n\\n      - name: Set up Go\\n        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\\n        with:\\n          go-version-file: go.mod\\n\\n      - name: Verify specification-to-code ownership\\n        run: go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\\n\\n      # The diff proves the committed catalog matches generator output, but\\n      # `go generate` runs nothing when its directive is disarmed: rewriting\\n      # `//go:generate` as `// go:generate` preserves the token while turning\\n      # the directive into a plain comment, so generation is skipped and the\\n      # diff stays clean. The anchored check refuses that token-preserving\\n      # rewrite; only the exact directive form counts. A new directive\\n      # without a pin update reddens here (and in\\n      # TestGenerateDirectiveStaysRecognizedForm) instead of going unchecked.\\n      - name: Verify generated catalog is current\\n        run: |\\n          test \\\"$(grep -c '^//go:generate' internal/catalog/catalog.go)\\\" -eq 1\\n          go generate ./internal/catalog\\n          git diff --exit-code -- internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go\\n\\n      # The release roots are derived from internal/specpin and\\n      # internal/catalog inside the gate, never retyped here. Each -- PASS\\n      # guard below must match: a selector that runs nothing fails here\\n      # instead of passing silently.\\n      - name: Run pinned contract-version gates\\n        run: |\\n          set +e\\n          go test ./internal/cigate -run 'TestVerifyContractPreservationLive|TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities|TestDerivedSetsAreComplete|TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets|TestCheckAgreementRefusals|TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift' -count=1 -v > cigate-contracts.log 2>&1\\n          code=$?\\n          set -e\\n          cat cigate-contracts.log\\n          test $code -eq 0\\n          for gate in TestVerifyContractPreservationLive TestPinnedReleasesAgreeAcrossAuthorities TestDerivedSetsAreComplete TestCheckAgreementAdmitsIdenticalSets TestCheckAgreementRefusals TestCheckReleaseRootsRefusesDrift; do\\n            grep -q \\\"^--- PASS: ${gate}\\\" cigate-contracts.log\\n          done\\n\\n  lint:\\n    name: Linters (vet, Windows vet, gofmt)\\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\\n    timeout-minutes: 10\\n    steps:\\n      - name: Check out repository\\n        uses: actions/checkout@v7\\n\\n      - name: Set up Go\\n        uses: actions/setup-go@v7\\n        with:\\n          go-version-file: go.mod\\n\\n      - name: Vet\\n        run: go vet ./...\\n\\n      - name: Vet Windows build-tagged sources\\n        run: GOOS=windows go vet ./...\\n\\n      # gofmt lists only offending files, so a clean tree prints nothing.\\n      # The file count proves the scan was not empty; the log must then be.\\n      - name: Check formatting\\n        run: |\\n          count=$(find internal -name '*.go' | wc -l | tr -d ' ')\\n          echo \\\"go files scanned: ${count}\\\"\\n          test \\\"${count}\\\" -gt 0\\n          set +e\\n          gofmt -l internal > gofmt.log 2>&1\\n          code=$?\\n          set -e\\n          cat gofmt.log\\n          test $code -eq 0\\n          test ! -s gofmt.log\\n=====\\n=====\\n./LOGBOOK.md:161:- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\\n./task-board.config.json:426:          \\\"go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check\\\",\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_review-verdict-rev2.md:146:| `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | exit 0 |\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_review-verdict-rev3.md:114:| `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` | exit 0 |\\n./.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_reviewer-cr1.md:3:Verify with your own instruments: (1) Whole-Story diff — story_final: the candidate tree against trunk e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311 is the complete Story delta: four replayed checkpoints (2u34k1, 1tvg8e, 2ez769, z1yxg9 — originals efe119a, 5e54874, ae5a4cc, 244a7dc) plus this leaf; confirm every replayed commit is signed and its tree equals the original except LOGBOOK.md (resolutions kept every entry newest-first, trunk's 3lt2xv entry preserved); run the stale-copy audit yourself: for every path in `git diff --name-only 62d4463 e4e3e88` confirm the candidate does not revert trunk content (README -adopted docs, LOGBOOK 3lt2xv entry, internal/catalog/*); task-board.config.json equals trunk plus only the z1yxg9 rpcwire fuzz gate (state the exact diff); this leaf is test-only plus traceability/README/LOGBOOK — confirm no production file changed. (2) AC-HOST-001 — extract the acceptance row text yourself and map each clause to the suite: full mutual TLS, exact enrolled certificate/UUID/hello, no preauthentication effects, migration/downgrade refusals, fresh-key rotation, revocation of idle/live streams within one second, expiry, concurrent mutation-generation fencing, valid and invalid actual certificates, both role failures, stale/failed reads, recovery bypasses; the producer reports 14 of 15 rows driven and B8 (revocation ≤ 1 s) partial: next-dispatch fence and WatchGeneration measured < 1 s but idle-without-traffic self-close NOT satisfied — decide from the pinned text whether \\\"revocation of idle/live streams within one second\\\" is met by a caller-polled WatchGeneration design (z1yxg9's stated bound) or requires an in-package idle close: if the latter, grade P2 and say whether a minimal RED-first product change in internal/hostchannel belongs to this Story before story_final (the leaf may carry it) — do not accept a stated bound that contradicts a MUST. (3) Hostile matrix through the real channel — rerun the seven hostile rows and then plant your own vectors: unknown root, re-issued leaf under an enrolled root, spoofed hello ID with a valid cert, SAN naming another UUID, destination mismatch, disconnect at each phase boundary (assert no durable write via a state-dir census), replayed TLS flight and replayed hello (assert the class), oversize frames (state which cap fires), disclosure mismatch (contracts.rpc, Error version drift), silent peer past handshake/hello deadlines, mid-request stall against the RPC timeout, two concurrent connections from one peer, copied key authenticating until revoked, rotation admitting the new tuple only after enrollment with retire_at bounds, stale generation at dispatch and at a mutation boundary under concurrent mutation, Config-4 legacy route / RPC-4 hello / plaintext preface refusals, both role failures, unreadable trust store = integrity failure, retry with changed operation ID/body refused; each with the exact Section 15 class/exit. (4) OpenSSH loopback lane — rerun hostile_carrier_test.go: it must start an unprivileged sshd on 127.0.0.1 with a temp host key and a forced command, observe the exact ServeArgv server-side, prove TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr; if it skips on this host the skip reason must be asserted and truthful; native Tailscale SSH must be recorded as not executed, never passed. (5) HC-* gates 10/10 with positive+negative vectors; the two z1yxg9 P3s closed (ax-host/2 same-family ALPN refused; bad-destination deadline hook). (6) Mutation — rerun mutations.py in an isolated copy (9 new + 26 prior probes; neutral passes; the documented client-cache SURVIVED), rerun each KILLED twice, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on the new assertion families (state-dir census ignoring one directory; disconnect classification collapsing transport_failure into authentication_failed; rotation admitting before enrollment for one peer; concurrent-mutation fence off by one generation) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control; per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, precise denominators. (7) Story-close items — ownership registry: AC-HOST-001 registered over the suite, new unevidenced bindings 11.10.1-11.10.4 + 16.1, 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed, 11.10.5 unowned by design; reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned over the merged registry (trunk rows + this Story's rows): recompute the projection digest independently, confirm every claimed clause line exists and each binding names an existing declaration driven by an acceptance case (plant a self-minted claim — refused), tracecheck counts reproduced; README/hostchannel README with test commands and no capability claim (no ax command); LOGBOOK newest-first with every Story entry plus trunk's 3lt2xv. (8) Hygiene — changed_paths carry no __pycache__/.pyc/stray plants or leftover sshd state; gofmt/vet clean; go test ./internal/hostchannel ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hosttrust ./internal/traceability/... -count=1 and -race green; tracecheck and `cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check` exit 0 on the exact tree.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 9819,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 2455,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
