{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000eb11","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b01d-784f-7181-a3b3-aa8522f5745f"},"sequence":5091,"recorded_at":1780531400010177,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5349c8a7-2a8a-407b-af90-af29b38e6bc7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b04a-d495-7220-9ae2-d29faa798c3a"},"task_id":"01a0b04a-d495-7220-9ae2-d29faa798c3a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b04a-d495-7220-9ae2-d29faa798c3a","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 6-8\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-## 2026-09-17\n-\n-### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\n+## 2026-09-17\n+\n+### TASK-260830-1geqhj — ax pane enforcement wrapper validation core (first leaf)\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/axpane` — the pure `Decide` core (`launch|reattach|attach_remote|takeover_offer|parked|refused`), the `Run` orchestration over real stores, the durable bootstrap `(session_id, bootstrap_operation_id)` binding store, §5.2 event authorship, and the §7.A descriptor builder. Every check composes a landed gate (`fencing`, `matjournal`, `sessckpt`/`sessrepo`, `sessprofile`, `provhost`, `resumesmoke`, `terminalbackend`, `config`, `axerror`); nothing is re-implemented. First leaf of STORY-260830-ptxkqe; `internal/traceability` untouched per the Story contract (final leaf re-pins).\n+- F1: `fencing` launch entries refuse — not park — foreign sessions, malformed tokens, and lapsed grants, so the wrapper's `refused(lease_conflict)` rows for foreign/expired inputs compose directly; only remote/ambiguous/unverified/absent/stale ownership parks. Remote parks resolve locally to `attach_remote` (interactive + attach admitted) or `takeover_offer`, and both offers still author `session.parked` with `remote_owner`.\n+- F2: the tuple gate must precede profile mapping in arm order: `ResolveMapping` re-checks the tuple internally, so mapping-first would wear tuple refusals as `profile_mapping_unavailable`. The standalone `CheckResumeTuple` call stays as fail-fast ordering; weakening it alone is unobservable (defense in depth, stated in TRACEABILITY.md).\n+- F3: `terminalbackend.Reconcile` maps generation drift to the more specific `terminal_backend_stale_generation` (not the generic mismatch), and `create` is conferred by both `durable_disconnect` and `headless_creation` — the unproven vector must deny both. `sessckpt.Get` re-attests through `sessrepo` on every read, so checkpoint admission composes through the read path.\n+- F4: `Bind` is linearizable on the commit race via link-EEXIST re-read (same operation reattaches to the winner, changed operation refuses); the `AfterStage` hook plays the concurrent winner deterministically in tests. The store stamps `created_at` itself — scalar timestamps require ≥3 fractional digits, so `time.RFC3339Nano` (which omits trailing zeros) is not a valid stamp.\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 24 narrowing mutants, all KILLED by named tests through `internal/axpane/mutant_harness.py`, plus the applied harmless SURVIVED control (24/24 rows match; per-plant raw logs with subprocess exits in the outcome tar). No token-preserving source-text mutant applies: no gate inspects source text.\n+- AC: 39 of 39 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in `internal/axpane/TRACEABILITY.md`); crash/idempotency evidence via the no-replace + fsync + hooks + real-kill pattern. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+\n+### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\n","final_result":true}}}
